**How to run the firewall**

Create a python environment
python3 -m venv firewall-env
source firewall-env/bin/activate

Install required

sudo pip3 install scapy netfilterqueue hping3

These two commands are critical to make your firewall work because they tell Linux to send packets through your Python script instead of letting them pass normally.

sudo iptables -I INPUT -j NFQUEUE --queue-num 1
sudo iptables -I OUTPUT -j NFQUEUE --queue-num 1

 sudo python3  firewall.py

You will start to see     🔥 NetfilterQueue-based Firewall is running… (Ctrl+C to stop)

Then from another terminal 

sudo hping3 -S -a 192.168.30.50 -p 80 192.168.30.128

It will be spoof ip and send as it is sent through 192.168.30.50 but it is actually sent from 192.168.30.128 which is your machines ip 

Then you will be seeing ❌ Dropped packet from 192.168.30.50 to 192.168.30.128:80
in firewall terminal.

ping 127.0.0.1

